4965a6c44c40364192b6620c5d31b60964925e20.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 24 at 11:39AM MDT until October 25 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Saturday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-24T23:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 242350 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 550 PM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flooding is ongoing across portions of southeast Utah and southwest Colo